[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human HCC normal (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=8,102): skew = -0.268, excess kurtosis = -0.328, D'Agostino K^2 p = 2.11e-32, Jarque-Bera p = 1.17e-29
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.324, excess kurtosis = 0.135, D'Agostino K^2 p = 2.53e-31, Jarque-Bera p = 7.05e-33
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 167.837, p = 6.44e-12
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 24.106, p = 3.65e-11
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
